; jpeg-encode — encodes a decoded JPEG description as a baseline sequential JPEG file.
;
; The value is the shape jpeg-decode produces: a dict with "header" (width, height,
; precision and components), "pixels" (a vector of rows, each a vector of
; (vector r g b) pixels) and "meta" (format and channel count).
;
; Pixels are converted to YCbCr with the JFIF transform and encoded as three
; components with no chrominance subsampling (4:4:4), so the encoder cannot recover
; a file's original sampling factors: what it emits is always 4:4:4.  Block edges
; are padded by repeating the last row and column.
;
; The quantisation and Huffman tables are the standard Annex K ones, the
; quantisation tables scaled for quality 95 (the IJG scaling rule), which keeps the
; re-encoding loss small enough for the round-trip suite to assert a tight
; tolerance.  There is no quality input because the value shape has nowhere to
; carry one.
;
; JPEG is lossy, so unlike the other codec pairs in this library
; (decode (encode v)) is not exactly v: it is the same size, with the same channel
; count, and within the tolerance the round-trip suite asserts.

